cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use VisionAssist in research or a project, please cite it."
title: "VisionAssist: Offline-first Hindi AI vision assistant for blind and visually impaired people"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: "techakash32"
repository-code: "https://github.com/techakash32/Hindi-multimodal-vision-assistant"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
abstract: >-
  VisionAssist is an open-source, offline-first assistive vision system that speaks Hindi.
  It detects nearby objects with YOLOv8, reads printed text with OCR, describes scenes with
  a vision-language model, and responds to offline Hindi voice commands.
keywords:
  - assistive technology
  - accessibility
  - Hindi
  - visually impaired
  - computer vision
  - offline AI
  - text to speech
  - OCR
  - YOLOv8
